# capability-composer live probe credentials (copy to .env — NEVER commit)
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then fill in the real keys. .env is gitignored.
#
# The live probe (scripts/live_probe.py) is OPT-IN: without a key it stays
# inert (exit 0, nothing attempted, sandbox stays the verified path). With a
# key it makes EXACTLY ONE read-only call against the real API and writes a
# §8 evidence artifact to evidence/live/ (content-addressed, polarity
# SUPPORTING on success / CONTRADICTING on failure).
#
# Where each key comes from:
#   GHL_API_KEY       GoHighLevel — Location API key (Settings > API Access)
#   HUBSPOT_API_KEY   HubSpot — Private App access token (Settings > Integrations
#                     > Private Apps); needs contacts+deals read scopes
#   SLACK_API_KEY     Slack — Bot token (xoxb-...) from your app's
#                     OAuth & Permissions page; needs channels:read, users:read
#
# Run (reads the real APIs once each, READ-ONLY — never creates/updates):
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   python scripts/live_probe.py
#
# Then feed the artifacts into the verification ledger:
#   skill-os replay-events   # (or the consumer directly — see the
#                            #  sovereign-verification SKILL.md)
GHL_API_KEY=
HUBSPOT_API_KEY=
SLACK_API_KEY=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sandbox WRITE verification (scripts/write_probe.py) — structurally separated
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The write probe reads *_SANDBOX_API_KEY ONLY (never the production keys
# above). It performs create -> read-verify -> delete -> verify-gone on a
# DEDICATED sandbox account and writes a §8 evidence artifact to
# evidence/write/ — evidence is emitted only for a complete round trip.
#
# Safety invariants (machine-checked):
#   * sandbox key absent + matching prod key present -> REFUSE (exit 2) — the
#     write probe never runs against a production credential
#   * sandbox key absent, no prod key -> inert (exit 0, nothing attempted)
#   * any leg fails (create / verify / delete / verify-gone) -> CONTRADICTING
#     evidence + exit 1 (fail loud) — a leave-behind is an incident, not a pass
#   * --dry-run prints the plan with no network; never wired into CI
#
# Use keys from a dedicated sandbox/test account — never production:
#   GHL_SANDBOX_API_KEY       GoHighLevel Location API key (test sub-account)
#   HUBSPOT_SANDBOX_API_KEY   HubSpot Private App token (test portal)
#   SLACK_SANDBOX_API_KEY     Slack Bot token (test workspace)
#   SLACK_SANDBOX_CHANNEL     the test channel the bot is in (message round trip)
#
# Run:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   python scripts/write_probe.py                # all sandbox-keyed providers
#   python scripts/write_probe.py --providers ghl --dry-run   # plan only
GHL_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
HUBSPOT_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
SLACK_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
SLACK_SANDBOX_CHANNEL=
